CM_ "v54 update: Added explicit TVMS Rouge label-page decode for raw CAN ID 0x17FD0430. Label item 0x17 is InputCurrent, supporting the 0x1BFD0230 D1=0x16 D3/10 A input-current candidate.";
CM_ "v56 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor configured-capacity decode. Config write raw CAN ID 0x0F0008FA uses D5-D6 little-endian Ah; status echo raw CAN ID 0x13F10008 uses D2-D3 little-endian Ah. Confirmed from battery 450ah - 350 - 400.csv sequence 450, 400, 350, 400 Ah.";
CM_ "v57 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor max charge current decode. Config write raw CAN ID 0x0F0008FA with D1=0x14 uses D5-D6 little-endian A; status echo raw CAN ID 0x13F10008 uses D5 raw A. Confirmed corrected sequence 20, 14, 10, 30 A.";
CM_ "v58 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor alarm config writes. Raw CAN ID 0x0F0008FA D1=0x41 uses D5-D6 little-endian percent for low SOC alarm; D1=0x42 uses D5-D6 little-endian millivolts for low voltage alarm. Confirmed sequences 10,15,20,30% and 10.0,11.0,11.5,12.0 V.";
CM_ "v59 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor alarm report fields on raw CAN ID 0x13F10A08. D2 reports low SOC alarm percent; D3-D4 little-endian millivolts report low voltage alarm. Confirmed around write transitions in more battery config.csv.";
CM_ "v60 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor SOC calibration target command. Raw CAN ID 0x0F0008FA D1=0x15 uses D5-D6 little-endian percent; calibrate battery start of charge full 5 times.csv captured five repeats of 100%.";
CM_ "v61 update: Added confirmed Battery Sensor battery type decode. Config write raw CAN ID 0x0F0008FA D1=0x11 uses D5-D6 little-endian type; status raw CAN ID 0x13F10008 D1 reports type. Mapping: 0=Gel, 1=AGM, 2=LeadAcid, 3=Calcium, 4=Lithium.";
CM_ "v62 update: Added confirmed Manager30 vehicle input trigger decode. Config write raw CAN ID 0x0F0001FA uses D1=0x68, D3=0x03, D5-D6 little-endian trigger; status raw CAN ID 0x03F20601 reports trigger in D8. Mapping: 0=Auto, 1=12V, 2=24V, 3=Ignition, 5=On.";
CM_ "v63 update: Added confirmed Redvision Display setting-change broadcast decode. Raw CAN ID 0x0F00FF20 from source 0x20 uses D1 as setting ID and D5-D6 little-endian value for battery type, capacity, max charge current, low SOC alarm, low voltage alarm, and vehicle input trigger.";
CM_ "v64 update: Added unconfirmed TVMS master command entries based on config/label pages: TVMS1280 item/channel 0x0F is Master switch, TVMS Rouge item/channel 0x0B is Master. ESPHome exposes them as HA switches using the existing TVMS on/off command shape.";
CM_ "v65 update: Added ESPHome test entities for TVMS1280 digital inputs 1-3. Channel map supplied by user: digital inputs are 0x01-0x03, outputs are 0x04-0x0D, inverter is 0x0E, master is 0x0F. Live-state PGN is still candidate; current test path uses 0x1BFD0024 channel feedback.";
CM_ "v66 update: Confirmed TVMS Rouge physical input/button states on 0x1BFD0030. D1=0x01 maps D2-D8 to inputs/buttons 1-7; D1=0x08 maps D2 to input/button 8. State values: 0x00 inactive, 0x01 active. 0x1BFD1430 remained idle in this test and is retained only as output/dimming activity status.";
CM_ "v67 update: Added Manager30 charging mode and charging stage decode. RedVision 0x0F00FF20 D1=0x43 D5 sets mode: 0=Touring, 1=Storage. Manager30 0x03F10801 D1 bit0 confirms mode. Manager30 0x03F20001 D1 reports stage: 0x21=Soft-start, 0x30=Boost, 0x40=Absorption, 0x70=Float. 0x4D remains a charge-cycle/stage request candidate.";

CM_ SG_ 2617049636 TVMS1280_Temp2_C "NOTE: TVMS1280 voltage inputs are item/channel 0x11 and 0x12 within the 0x1BFD0224 mux 0x11 page. Voltage Input 1 is D2-D3 millivolts, Voltage Input 2 is D4-D5 millivolts.";
CM_ SG_ 2617049636 TVMS1280_Temp1_C "NOTE: Temp1 is MUX 0x14 D2. Voltage Input 2 is not on this page; it is item/channel 0x12 in MUX 0x11 D4-D5 millivolts.";

CM_ "TVMS1280_DIGITAL_INPUTS_NOTE: Hardware has 3 digital inputs mapped to channels 0x01, 0x02, and 0x03. ESPHome exposes candidate binary sensors from 0x1BFD0024 channel feedback for field testing. A one-at-a-time input toggle capture is still needed before marking the live-state decode confirmed.";
